Notice for internal/dom

Go files in this directory follow or name source files of Blink, the layout
engine of Chromium. The license of each Blink file was read from the header
of the file at the tag 156.0.8078.4 of
https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src, the version of the reference
browser.

  xml.go             A port of markup_accumulator.cc and markup_formatter.cc
                     (BSD-2-Clause, with the copyright of Apple and Google
                     in the files).
  node.go            One function follows a function of element.cc
                     (LGPL-2.0-or-later). The file also ports parts of
                     d3-selection 3.0.0 (ISC).
  purify_support.go  Two functions follow functions of element.cc
                     (LGPL-2.0-or-later). The node iterator follows the DOM
                     standard. The class of Blink for it is in
                     node_iterator.cc (LGPL-2.0-or-later). The Go file does
                     not say that it follows that Blink file.
  selector.go        One comment names a rule of selector_checker.cc
                     (LGPL-2.0-or-later).
  style.go           A port of the method selection.style of d3-selection
                     3.0.0 (ISC).

parse.go and serialize.go port no upstream file.

NOTICE-Blink.txt in this directory has the first comment of each of these
Blink files, with its copyright lines. The text of the GNU Library General
Public License, version 2, is in ../browser/LICENSE-LGPL-2.0.txt.

The owner of the repository has not decided what to do with the code that
follows the LGPL files. The options are in docs/LICENSE-AUDIT.md, finding
F1. This notice states where the code comes from. It does not put the Go
files under a license.
